{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And your issue — your sons or your sons' sons who were born to you after you came, during these seventeen years that I have been here: they shall be called by the name of their brothers, and they shall not be tribes but rather fathers' houses. For all seventy persons who were present at the time of Jacob's coming — whether sons or sons' sons — were fathers' houses, and to them the land was apportioned, as we say in Bava Batra, and as is written in Pinchas: even among the sons of Perez — לְחֶצְרוֹן מִשְׁפַּחַת הַחֶצְרֹנִי לְחָמוּל מִשְׁפַּחַת הַחֲמוּלִי. And likewise among the sons of Bela — Arad and Naaman, etc. And it is written at the end: לָאֵלֶּה תֵחָלֵק הָאָרֶץ בְּנַחֲלָה וגו' לְשְׁמוֹת מַטּוֹת אֲבֹתָם יִנְחָלוּ. And likewise the sons of Joseph's sons who were born afterward shall be called by the name of their brothers in their inheritance and shall be fathers' houses, as is written in the section of Pinchas."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads 'your issue' as applying to both sons and grandsons born during the seventeen years Jacob spent in Egypt, paraphrasing the elliptic Hebrew syntax into explicit reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:32.792596838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}